  BSD 3-Clause licence: https://github.com/xenia-project/xenia/blob/master/LICENSE

mspack/ — the LZX decompressor and AES implementation, as Xenia vendors them in
`lib/mspack`. Headers here are byte-identical to that copy, including the `config.h`
that lets it build with no configure step.

  lzxd.c, lzx.h, mspack.h, readbits.h, readhuff.h, system.c, system.h, config.h
  libmspack — Copyright Stuart Caie and contributors
  GNU Lesser General Public Licence 2.1; the text is in mspack/COPYING.LIB, and the
  sources are here in full, so you can modify them and rebuild (`make -C ..`).

  rijndael-alg-fst.c, rijndael-alg-fst.h
  Optimised ANSI C Rijndael, version 3.0, by Vincent Rijmen and Paulo Barreto — see
  the notice at the top of the file.

TinySHA1.hpp — header-only SHA-1, Copyright (c) 2012-22 Saurav Mohapatra, based on
boost::uuid::details; permissive licence, notice in the file.

Everything else in this repository splits three ways.

`patches/offline.patch.json` is generated from, and `tools/stfs.py`, `tools/tongaspak.py`,
`tools/wbr.py`, `tools/lua51.py` are copies of, files from:

  Doritos Crash Course 1 & 2 in Xenia
  https://github.com/Lken-cmd/doritos-crash-course-xenia
  Copyright (c) 2026 Doritos Crash Course Xenia mod contributors
  MIT licence

`pakedits.py` is generated from that repository's `tools/build_cc2.py` — only the seven
template edits a console build needs, and its header records which copy.

This project wrote the console-specific parts — `revive.py`, `xexpatch.py`, `pakpatch.py`,
`check_hashes.py`, `verify_build.py`, both `Makefile`s, `xexmerge.cc` and `logstub.cc` —
under MIT, see `../../LICENSE`.

Note that the patch addresses in `patches/offline.patch.json` describe Doritos Crash
Course 2, which is EA's game: the licences here cover these scripts, not the game, and
this is meant for a copy you own.
